mantle rm196
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier full
written_for rm_godfrey_dripmore
title the stair gauge
fits stage=adult|old
prefers role=merchant job=crafter
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=frank piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk stacks_shards_to_measure_water_on_the_steps
likes fried_fish dancing market_bustle autumn_wind
dislikes haggling bad_manners
fears a_slick_step_beneath_a_loaded_tray
hopes dry_land_beyond_the_sound
topics work +0.6 land +0.4 pastimes +0.3 travel +0.3 gossip -0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=exact refuse=blunt tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# keeps broken crocks for measuring high water on the city steps, speaks frankly about a bad bargain and finds a dance partner by clearing space to turn.

words
oath! = Crocks afloat | A dry thumb on the sky
saying! = Stack a chip before you guess | A vessel tells on its maker
shard = a thumb of broken crock | a chip of glazed ware
blue = the blue chip | a shard blue as a beetle
rim = a flared lip | a generous rim
glaze = a pale glaze | a skin of green glaze
tray = my laden tray | the board I carry
ring = the clean note | a ringing sound
crack = a dull click | a sound like a shut drawer
tread = the worn tread | a hollow in the stair
gauge = a stack of chips | my little stair gauge
fry = a crisp fin | the crunchy bit beside the tail
beat = the second beat | a little lift in the tune
heel = my clumsy heel | the heel that always catches
windfall = a loose leaf | a curled leaf
burden = an awkward load | a tray that needs both paws
cloth = a damp rag | soft linen with a rubbed fringe
berth = a snug berth | a bunk no wider than a bench
runnel = the little watercourse | a groove between flags

any
opinion city for 2 : A hill tells you where your water went. That's one good feature of our town and welcome to it.
opinion dole for 2 : Fill the bowl. You can ask whose bowl it is after the poor wolf's eaten.
opinion merchants for 1 [self.role=merchant] : I mark every fault I know about and charge accordingly. Plenty of traders do as much.
opinion houses mixed 1 : I'd like a House to mend something small enough for an ordinary walker to notice.
opinion road against 1 [world.wagons=late] : My complaint is simple. A road that holds up the wagons needs work before it needs praise.
opinion strangers for 1 : If a stranger takes the other handle of a tray, I'll take the risk of asking a name.
opinion newcomers for 1 : Give a newcomer a corner to work in. A good corner can feed a whole family.
opinion watch for 1 : A steady paw directing carts does more good than three bright badges.
opinion festivals mixed 1 : Clear the floor and I'll dance. Fill it with speeches and I'll go looking for supper.

grown
line greet : Here beside me. There's firm footing here.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : Welcome. I've room enough to turn round with a stranger.
line greet [self.working=yes] : I'm listening even with my back bent over this.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : The light's thin yet. Step nearer while my eyes adjust.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. Nobody should have to feel for that last step.
line greet.return : Heard every syllable of that greeting. Glad to. | A good clear greeting carries.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Pull level with me and we'll have a proper word.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : One moment while I steady this. There.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening back. The edges of things vanish early.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : A steady paw for the far handle. You're welcome here.
line again.open : Back where our paths cross, I see.
line hail [pair.band=friends] : This side! More elbow room for my favourite company.
line farewell : Watch the turn on your way back down.
line farewell.return : Go carefully where stone's been polished smooth.
line react.news : Give me the words as near as you remember.
line react.news.new : That's the first chip of that story to reach me.
line react.news.known : Yes. The account I heard agrees so far.
line react.news.doubt : I'd set that one aside till another witness came along.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Hard hearing. I wish I had something useful to carry over.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Good. That's worth clearing a place at the table for.
line answer.how : Both feet under me and supper ahead.
line answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : Steady work. I'd welcome another pair of paws.
line ask.how : You've had a long enough pull today, by the look. How goes it?
line sympathise : You can set your load beside mine a while.
line reassure : Give it a minute to settle before you decide it's lost.
line thank : You got a grip where I couldn't. Much obliged.
line deflect_thanks : We had enough paws between us. That's all.
line decline : Excuse me from that. I promised to be somewhere else.
line accept_decline : That settles it, then. I'll make other arrangements.
line preclose [self.working=yes] : I'd best attend to the part that won't wait.
line preclose : I'll give you back the rest of your day.
line accept_preclose : Go along with an easy mind, then.
line ack : I follow the measure of it.
line give.advice : Check the footing before you put a second load on it.

scene chip_measure
when topic=weather here.weather=rain here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've stood three pot chips on edge down that runnel. | Rain's climbed halfway up #blue#. Didn't reach it on the last wet day.
b : To dam it? | What will you do when it does?
a : To see which one goes under first. Don't shift the blue. | Pick a higher step to carry things down, and let the next carrier know.


scene lowest_step
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does give.advice / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Test a slick step with your empty paw before you trust it with a full tray. | That hollow in the stone catches water first, ahead of every other stair.
b : Both paws are on the tray. | Deep enough to matter?
a : Exactly. That's why I go down once with nothing. | Deep enough to hide a loose edge. I'd sooner take the outside.


scene lid_seat
when topic=work self.working=yes self.job=crafter
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I can feel a crooked lid with my eyes shut. | If a lid sticks I look first for a grain of grit.
b : What gives it away? | Rather than forcing it?
a : It rocks against one claw. A good one settles without asking. | I've made enough fresh shards out of good pots by being impatient.


scene jug_lip
when topic=work self.job=crafter
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A jug gets its last test over my own boots. | I like a jug you can set down without a final drip.
b : You pour with your eyes closed? | Does that take a special shape?
a : I pour slowly. If my boot gets wet the lip needs work. | A clean edge below the spout. The water lets go there.


scene pottery_note
when topic=work self.job=crafter
does offer / react.self / assess
a : Tap that cup lightly. Hear #ring#? | I'd put this one out for buttons and that one out for broth.
b : Like a little bell. | They look alike to me.
a : Good. A hidden split swallows that note. | Listen to #crack#. Buttons won't seep out through a hairline.


scene dry_harbour
when topic=dreams|travel
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd take #berth# to see a place where chalk stays put a season. | My dream of travelling has one flaw. I want to cross the sea and arrive dry.
b : Could you sleep at sea? | Take spare stockings?
a : I expect I'd practise by rolling off my bench a few nights first. | A whole chest, if the dream has room.


scene dance
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dancing
does invite / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll dance one turn with you if you'll leave space for #heel#. | I keep missing #beat# when I watch the fiddler.
b : How much space? | Why watch at all?
a : The breadth of one toe. I learned the measure the hard way. | I'm wondering how so much of my trouble comes out of one elbow.


scene market
when topic=smalltalk here.place=market
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : Hear the square when two prices are called together. Almost a harmony. | In a busy market the hardest part's keeping a lane open.
b : Almost? | For all the carts?
a : Nobody on the lower note will shift. | For the little wolf with a bowl held out in front. Look low.


scene frying
when topic=food self.likes=fried_fish
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I leave #fry# to the end. Best proof the pan was hot. | A tang of hot butter will draw me away from a tune.
b : Better than the middle? | Before the dance is done?
a : Not better. Louder. | Between the dance and the bow. I do have manners.


scene haggling
when topic=prices self.role=merchant
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : I'd rather hear a straight refusal than three guesses at my price. | One good question about a fault is worth a morning's haggling.
b : What if the price is too high? | Does a fault come off the price?
a : Then say so and let me reckon whether I can do better. | Certainly. Looking sorry doesn't.


scene saltwind
when topic=season here.season=autumn
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : An autumn wind turns dry leaves into little sounders. | Look at #windfall# upright between two stones. Looks about to sail.
b : Sounders? | Where would it go?
a : They rattle on the shallow stones and stick where the holes are wet. | Downhill, if it's sense enough to follow the wagons.


scene rain_clear
when topic=weather here.weather=clear
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Fine clear spell. I can see the silt line on #tread#. | I'll put #blue# back in my pocket while the sky's clear.
b : High this time? | You'll lose your mark.
a : High enough that I'd have come up the other way. | There's a pale patch where it sat. The sun keeps my place for half a day.


scene family
when topic=family self.married=yes
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : For #self.spouse# I'd save a cup that sits nicely in the paw. | My idea of an evening with #self.spouse# has room in it for silence.
b : Prettiest one? | No dancing?
a : I said nicely. An ugly one might be the very thing. | You don't have to talk to keep time together.


scene crooked_cup
when topic=pastimes
does give.opinion / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like an odd cup on a table of matching ones. | There ought to be one chipped dish kept in every house.
b : So you can see which is yours? | What's it good for?
a : So the odd guest can see there's room. | The task that would make you anxious with a fine dish.


scene news
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.gossip / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The account I've heard is that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | I hear #topic.subject# #topic.claim#.
b : Do you put any faith in it? | Is that the whole account?
a : Enough to listen twice. I'd need more to say it's true. | That's the only piece I can lay my paw on.


scene wagons
when topic=caravan world.wagons=raided
does tell.worry / react.self / assess
a : Raided wagons mean a lot more waiting. I pity those waiting for ordinary things. | I won't make a tale of the raid. There's a tale enough in an empty yard.
b : What ordinary things? | What can one do?
a : A shoe to fit. A handle for a door. A crock that keeps broth where it belongs. | Lend what one has till another load comes in.


scene lean
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does give.opinion / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Hard times teach you what the chipped things are good for. | Lean season. I like a pot that can do two jobs now.
b : Even the ones with holes? | Which two jobs?
a : An herb pot wants a drain. Even a broken base can earn its keep. | Carry a meal to a neighbour and bring something useful back.


scene hall_sound
when topic=lore here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The steps through the Commons each give a footfall a different sound. | A shout from above sounds quite different from one down by the market.
b : Could you find the way by ear? | Which travels further?
a : Part of it. I'd still want a lookout for wagon wheels. | The one that says to get clear. We all lend it an ear.


scene raised_bowl
when topic=work self.job=crafter
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm trying a bowl on a foot high enough to leave room for a cloth. | A pot doesn't need feet as long as its maker's, but it does need balance.
b : So the table stays dry? | How do you judge?
a : So a pup can slip a paw under and lift without spilling. | Put it on a board with a pea under one corner. See if it sulks.


scene rough_lug
when topic=work self.job=crafter
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I put a thumb hollow into the clay of a soft handle. | I leave the handle rougher than the belly.
b : To show who made it? | A rough pot's not much use.
a : To tell a tired paw where to rest. | A rough handle's different. It gives wet claws somewhere to catch.


scene festival
when topic=festival
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At a festival I look for the dancers who have lost the tune. | A good tune makes even an empty bowl worth having.
b : To put them right? | For catching coins?
a : To dance alongside and pick it up together. | For beating the time softly with a knuckle.


scene wayside
when topic=newcomer
does give.advice / react.self / assess
a : To a newcomer I'd show the handrails first. | Somebody should mark reliable steps with a dab of colour.
b : Before the inns? | So strangers can find them?
a : Yes. You have to reach the inn in one piece. | So anybody carrying too much can follow without asking.


scene honest
when topic=friends
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I trust a friend who'll point out a wobble on the table. | You know who's good company when a carrying handle snaps.
b : Even at supper? | The one who catches the load?
a : Especially with a full dish coming down. | Or stays to gather the pieces. Anybody can shout.


scene clay_sleep
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dreamt the whole hill was spinning and I had to hold it steady. | I dreamt of a field with all the rain lying next door.
b : Did you manage? | What was the boundary?
a : One paw on the top. In the morning I'd wrapped the blanket round a bedpost. | A row of lids, each one tipped just so.


scene rainword
when topic=weather here.weather=fog
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Mist rounds off every edge I use to find my way. | You can see wet on the ground before you see the thing that dripped.
b : What guides you through it? | What's above us?
a : The kerb against my toes. Goes on being a kerb in any weather. | Stand back a pace. There's the end of a gutter in the murk.


scene elbowroom
when topic=home
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : A table suits me when I can walk all round it. | I measure a good doorstep in paw-widths.
b : To carry dishes away? | A generous doorstep, then?
a : To draw up one more seat where nobody expected room. | Generous enough to put the parcel down and still open the door.


scene two_sides
when topic=faith
does give.opinion / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I remember the Bright One best when a simple thing gives years of service. | A quiet hour's a decent offering.
b : Do you ask a blessing first? | Who gets the benefit?
a : Sometimes. I still check for leaks. | Try to hear which of my neighbours could use it more.


scene sparing_water
when topic=land
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll pour a little water to see which way the ground lies. | If you want to find the low corner, send a drop first.
b : Can't you tell by looking? | Just one?
a : I can guess. Water gives an answer without guessing. | Less mopping to do if the low corner's under your bed.


story dry_sketch [topic=memories|travel self.age>=30]
  : I once drew a view of a dry coast beneath the rim of a saucer.
  : I packed it very carefully and then put the saucer down and forgot which it was.
  b : How did you find your coast again?
  : By finishing my supper and doing the washing up. Shortest sea journey I've made.


story fish_tune [topic=memories|food]
  : A fiddler once played for a cook who'd promised a plate of fried fish.
  : Each time the tune ended the cook turned the fish. Each time the fish turned the fiddler started again.
  b : Who gave in first?
  : The fish. The skin fell off into the pan and they both stopped to eat it.


story stair_line [topic=memories here.region=ridgemere]
  : Once I stacked white chips on the low stair where the drains run together.
  : By the time I came back the water was gone and a pup had built a palace with the chips.
  b : Did you take it apart?
  : No. I put the water mark on the palace wall. Better than my heap by far.


story first_bowl [topic=memories|work self.job=crafter]
  : My first bowl had one side much lower than the other.
  : I kept it hidden until an old gardener asked for a dish a fledgling could drink from.
  b : The low edge came in useful?
  : Just the height of a small beak. I wish I'd had the sense to make it so on purpose.


story dropped_tray [topic=memories self.age>=25]
  : I slipped once with a tray full of cups. Got the tray level on the way down.
  : Not a cup tipped. I'd just begun to feel proud when my rump hit the cobbles.
  b : That finished the trick?
  : The whole tray bounced. I learned to carry less from one place to the next.


rule @water
when concept=bark here.weather=rain here.region=ridgemere
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Mind the stair with the white chip! | Upper edge is sound. Take a short stride.


rule @pot
when concept=bark self.job=crafter working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Turn the handle towards the rim. There. | Listen to the hollow note in that one.


rule @dancer
when concept=bark self.likes=dancing
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Leave one board bare for the dancers! | I can hear the beat in that shuffle of feet.


rule @fish
when concept=bark self.likes=fried_fish
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Keep that crisp edge for me! | Smells like the pan's hot enough at last.


rule @market
when concept=bark here.place=market
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Set the heavy bundle over here till the lane opens! | Let a little daylight through for the caller at the back.


rule @season
when concept=bark here.season=autumn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Wind has swept every leaf into the hollow. | That gust gives the high branches a good airing.

dlg resident.hub : Come level with me. I like to hear a question straight.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, I see you've found my usual perch.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : We'll manage a civil word with a bit of space between us.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : Keep the lamp between us so I can see what you mean.
dlg resident.job [self.job=crafter] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. Any pot I send out ought to earn its shelf space.
dlg resident.job : I'm happiest at work that gives me something solid to show at the end.
dlg resident.business [business=steady] : Things sit level at present. I'm content to have it that way.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : #world.news#. I had it by way of #world.news_from#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : I've been told #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Go carefully with it.
dlg resident.bye : Take the route that gives you the surest footing.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop!=bare] : Come within reach. It's easier to judge with your own paws.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop!=bare topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, you know I give straight answers about stock.
dlg shop.prices : I'll show you what the extra work went into. Decide for yourself if it's worth the price.
dlg shop.bye : Carry anything delicate up against your chest.

graft resident.hub
choice Why stack chips on a step? -> stair_stack
node stair_stack
say Water takes the lower ones first. If the top one goes under, I tell anyone with a heavy load to walk round another way.
mood keen
choice Why choose chips? -> cheap_mark
choice I'll watch the upper chip. -> hub
node cheap_mark
say A broken cup still has work to do. I like a measure I can afford to lose.
choice Good use for it. -> bye

graft shop.greet
choice Could I try the weight? -> weight_hand
node weight_hand
say Certainly. Turn your paw as if you were tipping something out. You feel the weight move.
choice Why does that matter? -> tip_test
choice I've felt enough. -> greet
node tip_test
say What feels light on a shelf can drag when you have it at an angle. I'd sooner have you learn it here than after you paid.
choice I'll bear that in mind. -> greet
